Hello, I am yet another happy ALSA user.
  I own a SBLive! Value and I want to load patchs into the DSP. The main
thing I need to do is invert the rear channels because they are
canceling out the base in my sub-woofer, but reverb and stuff would be
very cool. Has any one had success with this? Is there any software to
do it? I saw mention of a program called ld10k1 on the 'net. I emailed
the author, but have yet to receive a responce.
  I suspect (from I've seen on the 'net) that there is no good way to do
this (in ALSA). If this is true, it needs to be remedied. I am a
programmer and I have thought about trying my hand at writing a program
to load DSP patchs (a'la emu-dspmgr from the OSS drivers), but I have
absolutly no knowlege of how to write a linker, so I would need help.
  So my question is: Is there any work being done on this? If so, can I
help? If not, can someone help me get started on this project?

Thanks.

